From ebc48df6701d563f06a7a56c8cb4fab41b63c697 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VPinInfinite <340424849+VPinInfinite@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] pinone: the PinOne Ultra's USB HID vendor channel, from
 DirectOutput pull request #27

Ported from Cleveland Software Design's change to DirectOutput (pull request
#27 at c5ae628, MIT) for Visual Pinball Infinite: current PinOne firmware takes
DOF's output packets on its USB HID vendor channel (VID 0x39F5, PID 0x9208,
usage page 0xFF00, usage 0x01, report 6, 64-byte reports) instead of a virtual
COM port. A PinOne configured with ComPort HID writes there. The
auto-configurator looks for the HID channel first, then for an older board's
port by its USB IDs (VID 0x0E8F, PID 0x9207) instead of probing every serial
port, scanning them all only when the port list can't be read, then asks the
named-pipe server, as the pull request's C# does.

Where hidapi differs from the C#'s Win32 calls: hidapi doesn't hand out
Windows' error number, so a failed write tries reopening the handle on any
error, not only on "invalid handle"; the port's USB IDs come from
libserialport where the C# asks WMI.
